## 3. Model specification

The Day 3 DCM used the verified Day 2 model structure.

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Analysis | ERP |
| Neural mass model | CMC |
| Spatial model | IMG |
| Conditions | Standard and Pitch Deviant |
| Condition coding | Standard = 0, Pitch Deviant = 1 |
| Time window | -100 to 300 ms |
| Spatial modes | 8 |
| Hanning window | On |
| Receptor-informed priors | No |

### Sources

| Index | Source | MNI coordinate |
|---:|---|---|
| 1 | left A1 | [-42 -22 7] |
| 2 | right A1 | [46 -14 8] |
| 3 | left STG | [-61 -32 8] |
| 4 | right STG | [59 -25 8] |
| 5 | left IFG | [-46 20 8] |
| 6 | right IFG | [46 20 8] |

### Connectivity structure

- **A matrix:** baseline extrinsic connectivity across the auditory hierarchy.
- **B matrix:** Pitch Deviant modulation relative to Standard.
- **C matrix:** auditory driving input to bilateral A1.

Conceptually:

```text
left A1  <-> left STG  <-> left IFG
right A1 <-> right STG <-> right IFG
left IFG <-> right IFG
```

The condition-specific connectivity is:

```text
Standard connectivity      = A
Pitch Deviant connectivity = A + B
```

