## 7. Key interpretation

The Day 3 baseline CMC DCM was successfully inverted and passed visual fit-quality inspection. The fitted model reproduced the main temporal and spatial structure of the grand-average MEG responses for both Standard and Pitch Deviant conditions.

The model also produced interpretable parameter estimates:

- baseline A coupling followed the expected auditory hierarchy;
- B coupling showed condition-specific Pitch Deviant modulation;
- C coupling confirmed auditory input to bilateral A1 only;
- response and scalp-map plots showed no evidence of gross model failure.

The baseline model was therefore retained as the reference model for subsequent receptor-informed DCM comparisons.

The baseline model evidence value to preserve is:

```text
F_baseline = 64.2175
```

Future receptor-informed models will be compared using:

```text
Delta F = F_receptor_informed - F_baseline
```

